WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.200
Although many MCU characters show up more&nbsp;
than once, not every hero and villain gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.880
a comeback — despite what the actors&nbsp;
involved might want. But that doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:14.000
stop them from dreaming. These are the actors&nbsp;
who desperately want to return to the MCU.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.800
The second season of Netflix's Daredevil&nbsp;
introduced one of the vigilante hero's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:24.400
greatest supporting characters: Elektra, played by&nbsp;
Elodie Yung. She next appeared in The Defenders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.480
serving as an antagonist to Daredevil&nbsp;
and his reluctant teammates Luke Cage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:34.080
Iron Fist, and Jessica Jones. While Elektra's&nbsp;
latter appearance ended in her apparent demise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.800
anyone familiar with the character will know&nbsp;
that death rarely puts an end to her adventures.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.160
At the Wizard World Virtual Experiences&nbsp;
2020's Marvel Actors Panel, Yung expressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.760
enthusiasm at the prospect of&nbsp;
reprising her role. She said:

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.560
"Let me tell you, I love this&nbsp;
character because she's so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.200
complex and broken [...] She's got a lot of&nbsp;
villain in her [...] and also a lot of good."

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.680
Yung also shared how much&nbsp;
she liked working without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.680
knowing where her character arc would end up.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.440
"Marvel [Television], in my experience,&nbsp;
are very secretive. So from the moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.200
you start auditioning until the end of a&nbsp;
series, you never know where it's going."

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.680
Sadly, Yung couldn't say for&nbsp;
certain whether Daredevil's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.360
former flame would formally&nbsp;
debut in the MCU anytime soon.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.920
Before the deal between Sony and Marvel&nbsp;
made it possible for Spider-Man to become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.560
Iron Man's protege, there was Harley Keener.&nbsp;
Keener was the promising young inventor who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.360
helped Tony Stark get through his struggles&nbsp;
with trauma during the events of Iron Man 3.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.160
"I'm cold."

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.520
"I can tell. You know how I can&nbsp;
tell? Because we're connected"

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.360
However, it took six years for the character&nbsp;
to make another appearance in the MCU — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.160
a rather unexpected one, at that. He showed&nbsp;
up at Tony's funeral in Avengers: Endgame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:52.560
surprising many audiences who didn't&nbsp;
immediately recognize the teenaged Keener.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.040
In an interview with IGN, Simpkins mentioned how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.400
thrilled he was at the prospect&nbsp;
of reprising his role. He said:

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:03.280
"When they gave me the call that I was going to do&nbsp;
it, I was freaking out and screaming in the car."

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:08.240
Simpkins also explained that, at the time, his&nbsp;
return wasn't set in stone yet, so he refrained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:13.520
from telling anyone about it for fear of things&nbsp;
going sideways. Of course, Tony Stark's heroic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:19.840
sacrifice left a huge hole in the MCU — one that&nbsp;
Simpkins is more than willing to fill. When asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.400
about the possibility of Keener donning one of&nbsp;
Tony's suits and continuing Iron Man's legacy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:30.160
Simpkins exclaimed that he was 100% on board.&nbsp;
Interestingly, the time-traveling Young Avenger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:35.840
Iron Lad was also mentioned as an option; one&nbsp;
that Simpkins said he would do "without a doubt."

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.680
You'd be forgiven for thinking that&nbsp;
Sterling K. Brown's participation in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.800
the MCU was a one-and-done deal. After all,&nbsp;
his role in Black Panther was a brief one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.520
regardless of its significance to the plot.&nbsp;
Brown played the role of Prince N'Jobu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:54.960
the father of Erik Killmonger and uncle&nbsp;
of T'Challa. In his desire to extend aid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.960 --> 00:03:00.080
to marginalized people outside of the African&nbsp;
nation of Wakanda, N'Jobu works with Ulysses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:05.920
Klaue to smuggle out its most precious resource,&nbsp;
the unique metal called vibranium. N'Jobu is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.800
then killed after making an attempt on Zuri's&nbsp;
life. As such, barring any further flashback&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:15.760
sequences in future Black Panther movies, it&nbsp;
seems unlikely that N'Jobu will ever return.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.320
However, Brown isn't averse to the idea&nbsp;
of reprising his role in the MCU. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.440
fans asked about the chances of him&nbsp;
showing up in a future Marvel movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:27.120
the actor tweeted that he's open&nbsp;
to returning as N'Jobu, saying:

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.840
"If there's a way, I would&nbsp;
be honored #WakandaForever."

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:36.960
In the MCU, Josh Brolin lent his acting skills&nbsp;
and imposing frame to the intergalactic tyrant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:40.320
Thanos. By bringing the character&nbsp;
to life across multiple films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:45.360
Brolin cemented his place in MCU history as&nbsp;
one of its most significant players. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.040
Brolin played another fan favorite&nbsp;
Marvel character outside the MCU:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:54.000
the time-traveling mutant called Cable in&nbsp;
Deadpool 2. Since it's a 20th Century Fox&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.520
film, Deadpool 2 initially existed outside the&nbsp;
boundaries of Marvel's mainstream MCU continuity.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:04.480
Thanks to Disney's acquisition of Fox and the&nbsp;
MCU's ongoing exploration of the multiverse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.760
however, it now appears that pretty much anything&nbsp;
can happen. And if comics creator Rob Liefeld is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:15.280
to be believed, Brolin would be delighted to get&nbsp;
another shot at portraying the mutant gunslinger.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:20.400
ComicBook.com quoted Liefeld as saying that&nbsp;
Brolin was "itching to be Cable again," saying:

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.280
"He told me he understands how&nbsp;
beloved his role as Thanos is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.000
but he doesn't look completely like Josh Brolin."

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.600
Meanwhile, Brolin himself has revealed&nbsp;
in interviews that Cable's appearance in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:34.880
Deadpool 2 was only supposed to be the start of&nbsp;
the character's journey. Brolin told Ace Universe:

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:42.160
"I don't know what Marvel has in store, but it&nbsp;
turned out to be one really fun movie for me."

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.520
The MCU's version of the Red Guardian turned&nbsp;
out to be significantly different from his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.440
mainstream comic book counterpart. But&nbsp;
David Harbour, who brought the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:57.360
to life in 2021's Black Widow, didn't seem&nbsp;
to mind. In fact, as he later told Insider,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.720
he considers the role to be "one&nbsp;
of the biggest gigs" of his life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:05.520
And he's certainly willing to reprise it, should&nbsp;
Marvel ask him to come back. Harbour simply said:

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:06.880
"I'm down for more."

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:11.200
Harbour even suggested two ideas for&nbsp;
Red Guardian's next on-screen adventure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:15.840
In one scenario, audiences could get a glimpse&nbsp;
of Russia's own supersoldier through a number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.400
scenes depicting the Red Guardian in his prime.&nbsp;
Harbour's other idea for Red Guardian's return&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.120
features him going down the same road Yelena&nbsp;
did at the end of the film. Harbour said:

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:28.080
"When he finds out that [Natasha]&nbsp;
was on that cliff with Hawkeye and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:31.920
maybe the version of the story he hears is&nbsp;
that Hawkeye pushed her off or something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:37.120
it's a moment when Red Guardian turns back to&nbsp;
the guy he was. He now wants vengeance for her."

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:43.200
One of the most shocking twists in Black Widow&nbsp;
involved an alternative take on a classic Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:48.320
villain. Whereas the Taskmaster from the comics&nbsp;
is a highly skilled ex-S.H.I.E.L.D. operative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:53.120
named Tony Masters, the MCU version&nbsp;
of the acrobatic antagonist is Antonia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:58.080
Dreykov — the mind-controlled daughter of&nbsp;
the Red Room's overseer, General Dreykov.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:02.720
The conclusion of the 2021 film saw Dreykov&nbsp;
being set free from her father's grip after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:07.120
spending years as his mind-controlled assassin.&nbsp;
With this new development for the character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:11.760
Olga Kurylenko believes that there's more than&nbsp;
enough story potential to earn Taskmaster a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:16.080
spot on the MCU's roster of recurring&nbsp;
stars. In an interview with Slashfilm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.640
Kurylenko shared a few ideas about where&nbsp;
the character could go next. She said:

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:25.520
"It's always a danger to keep away from being&nbsp;
possessed and concentrate on keeping her freedom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:27.680
But it doesn't mean that she'll succeed at it. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.960
there's always bad forces that will&nbsp;
try to capture her, I would imagine."

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.800
Kurylenko added that she'd be more&nbsp;
than happy to reprise her role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.640
as she believes that Taskmaster is&nbsp;
"too valuable and too skillful [for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:43.360
Marvel Studios] to let go." She expressed the&nbsp;
same sentiment in an Esquire interview too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:47.840
but clarified that it's up to Marvel to decide&nbsp;
if she is to get another chance in the spotlight.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:52.000
In past interviews, Crossbones actor Frank Grillo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.160
hasn't been shy about speaking his mind&nbsp;
regarding Marvel's handling of his character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:01.360
in MCU films. During a 2021 appearance on the&nbsp;
Lights Camera Barstool podcast, for instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:06.720
Grillo shared why he was initially hesitant to&nbsp;
reprise his role in Avengers: Endgame, saying:

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:11.680
"I was a little pissed off about it, 'cos&nbsp;
I signed a seven picture deal with them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:15.920
and it was like 'oh, you're gonna be part of the&nbsp;
Marvel universe, right?' And it didn't happen."

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:20.960
However, Grillo has been equally candid about&nbsp;
how much he'd like to play Brock Rumlow again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:25.840
whether on the silver screen or on a Disney+&nbsp;
show. In an interview with Forbes, he said:

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:29.360
"I would love to do [a Crossbones series]&nbsp;
just because I have never seen a character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.360
be on the screen so little and yet have&nbsp;
such a fan following. [...] I have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.520
great relationship with Marvel and the guys there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:39.680
but why didn't they [...] pursue that? Why&nbsp;
isn't Crossbones somewhere in the mix?"

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:43.440
Grillo returned to voice Crossbones for&nbsp;
the Disney+ series What If...? — but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:47.760
by his own admission, he'd be just as&nbsp;
eager to suit up himself. As he said:

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:51.120
"Oh yeah. I often say 'When Marvel&nbsp;
calls, I pick up the phone.'"

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:57.040
The connection between the Netflix Marvel shows&nbsp;
and the MCU has always been tenuous at best,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:01.520
with Netflix's series only occasionally&nbsp;
referencing certain events from the films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:06.560
and the MCU movies completely ignoring the&nbsp;
TV shows. Still, that hasn't stopped Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:12.000
fans from hoping that the likes of Daredevil and&nbsp;
Jessica Jones could somehow be folded into the MCU&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:16.400
canon — mainly because of the masterful&nbsp;
way in which those characters were handled.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:21.680
For example, Vincent D'Onofrio's performance&nbsp;
as the iconic villain Kingpin made fans so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:26.560
happy that calls for him to reprise his role&nbsp;
in the MCU never seem to end. Based on an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:30.720
interview with Screen Rant, the actor himself&nbsp;
is just as keen on the prospect of returning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:34.800
After being asked about his rumored return&nbsp;
in the upcoming Hawkeye series on Disney+,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:39.760
D'Onofrio said that he "so badly" wants to&nbsp;
breathe life into Fisk's character again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:43.920
should Marvel Studios ever grant him&nbsp;
another opportunity. He continued:

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:47.520
"I just have to wait for Marvel to ask&nbsp;
me. I think it's very clear that I would,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:51.680
and the fans know that I would jump at the&nbsp;
chance to play again. I just need to be asked."

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:57.040
Marvel Studios and Kevin Feige have been&nbsp;
characteristically tight-lipped about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:02.400
status of the Netflix Marvel shows. Whenever the&nbsp;
question of reviving Netflix's hit shows crops up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:07.600
Feige's answers tend to be much like the one&nbsp;
he gave in a Deadline interview, when he said:

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:11.280
"I've been at Marvel long enough&nbsp;
to never say never about anything."

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:15.600
That said, if it were up to Jessica Jones star&nbsp;
Krysten Ritter, her character at least would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:20.480
be making her MCU debut, as she has claimed&nbsp;
that she'd "absolutely just die" to play the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:25.360
tough-as-nails private eye in an unquestionably&nbsp;
canonical Marvel Studios production.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:28.960
In an interview with Screen Rant, Ritter&nbsp;
claimed that Jessica Jones really struck a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.840
chord with female audiences, particularly&nbsp;
those who had survived abuse. She said:

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.640
"Not only because it was [...] a&nbsp;
great role and she's such a bad-ass,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:40.960
but that character has really resonated with&nbsp;
people in a way that I don't know who else has."

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:44.640
Ritter added that she would jump at the&nbsp;
chance to step into Jessica's shoes again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:47.760
should Marvel call on her&nbsp;
to do so. Luckily for her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:52.240
rumors have since surfaced that Ritter might&nbsp;
show up as Jones on the Disney+ She-Hulk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:57.200
series — so fans might just see the ill-mannered&nbsp;
investigator return sometime in the near future.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.200
Judging from the number of times&nbsp;
Daredevil star Charlie Cox has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:05.360
asked if he will reprise his Netflix role in&nbsp;
Spider-Man: No Way Home, it's probably fair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:10.000
to say that fans are hungry to see Hell's&nbsp;
Kitchen's greatest hero make his return.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.520
While the actor has been decidedly careful&nbsp;
about the way in which he responds to that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:17.840
particular question, Cox hasn't ruled&nbsp;
out any future appearances in the MCU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:21.360
In fact, he has even suggested a&nbsp;
number of ways in which Daredevil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:24.960
can integrate himself into the&nbsp;
MCU's version of New York City.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:28.560
In an interview with ComicBook.com,&nbsp;
Cox expressed gratitude at being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:32.000
able to portray Matt Murdock and&nbsp;
his alter-ego for three seasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:36.960
of the eponymous Netflix show. Moreover,&nbsp;
as a self-admitted fan of the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:41.680
Cox offered up some of his own ideas as&nbsp;
to how his character can return. He said:

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:45.120
"As a fan of the Marvel movies, I've&nbsp;
loved the little stuff where they pop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:48.800
up here and there [...] I love the idea&nbsp;
of Jessica [Jones] and Matt showing up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:53.600
in the background or Matt as a lawyer advising&nbsp;
Peter Parker. That'd be really, really cool."

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:57.200
Of course, given Spider-Man's imminent&nbsp;
legal troubles in No Way Home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:59.840
it's clear enough that he's going&nbsp;
to need all the help he can get...

